lazydocker is a terminal interface for viewing and managing Docker
containers, images, and volumes.

A running Docker daemon and the Docker CLI are required. Docker 29.7.2
was tested; older versions were not tested. The user must have access
to the Docker daemon. Access to the Docker socket grants root-equivalent
privileges. Docker Compose is optional for managing Compose projects.

The source archive includes vendored Go modules. The build does not
download dependencies. Go 1.23.6 or newer is recommended by upstream.
